# npm lockfile (project uses pnpm)
package-lock.json

# Package manager lock files (only commit the one you actually use)
# 
# CURRENT STATE (2026-01-06):
# - Project uses pnpm (see package.json scripts)
# - package-lock.json IS TRACKED (not ignored) because pnpm-lock.yaml doesn't exist yet
# - This ensures dependency reproducibility until pnpm migration is complete
#
# MIGRATION STEPS (when ready to switch to pnpm):
# 1. Run: pnpm install (generates pnpm-lock.yaml)
# 2. Uncomment the package-lock.json line below
# 3. Run: git rm --cached package-lock.json (remove from tracking)
# 4. Commit both changes together
#
# For pnpm projects – commit pnpm-lock.yaml, ignore the others
# package-lock.json    # ← CURRENTLY COMMENTED (package-lock.json is tracked)
# yarn.lock            # ← uncomment if you ever switch to yarn
!pnpm-lock.yaml        # ← explicitly allow pnpm-lock.yaml to be committed

